Do not release until the locale catalogues are imported into GlotPress.

Reason
------
1.29.8 stopped bundling .mo files, so every locale now comes from the
WordPress.org language pack, and those packs are built from
translate.wordpress.org.

1.30.0 replaced about 520 Polish source strings with English ones. Every msgid
on translate.wordpress.org for those strings is stale, for EVERY locale, not
only Polish. Until the new catalogues are imported there, the packs cannot
match them and each affected locale drops by roughly 520 strings, which is
below the threshold that gets a pack built at all.

Releasing before the import leaves Polish shops with an English interface,
including the statutory withdrawal instructions and the model withdrawal form,
and does the same to Czech, Slovak, Chinese and Belarusian.

What to import
--------------
These files are already rebuilt against the new msgids. They take
translate.wordpress.org as the source and only fill what it does not have, so
importing them does not overwrite community wording.

  languages/polski-pl_PL.po    100%   REQUIRED, has a pack today
  languages/polski-cs_CZ.po    100%   has a pack today
  languages/polski-sk_SK.po     94%   has a pack today
  languages/polski-zh_CN.po     94%   has a pack today
  languages/polski-bel.po       94%   has a pack today
  languages/polski-es_ES.po     97%   no pack today, Spanish falls back to English
  languages/polski-de_DE.po     97%   no pack today

Import into the dev/<locale>/default/ and stable/<locale>/default/ sub-projects
of https://translate.wordpress.org/projects/wp-plugins/polski/

es_ES and de_DE are AI-assisted, so a GTE may refuse them. See
plogins-plugins/GLOTPRESS-IMPORT.md before pushing those two.

How to clear this
-----------------
1. Import at least polski-pl_PL.po. Importing needs PTE, so no script can do it.
2. Confirm the packs rebuilt:

     curl -s "https://api.wordpress.org/translations/plugins/1.0/?slug=polski" \
       | python3 -c "import sys,json;[print(t['language'],t['version'],t['updated']) for t in json.load(sys.stdin)['translations']]"

3. Delete this file, commit the deletion, then run the release.

